WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.490
Welcome to Learn Text.js.

2
00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:06.740
This is chapter one: Getting Started.

3
00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:11.100
Over ten chapters, you'll
build Acme Deploys:

4
00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:14.730
a deploy dashboard that renders
in the DevTools console.

5
00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:18.250
Each chapter ends with the app
exactly as your code leaves it,

6
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.210
running live in the
console on the lesson page.

7
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:23.450
In this first one, you'll create the app,

8
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.100
render your first page,
and respond to a key.

9
00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.310
First, a quick look at how it works.

10
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:33.030
A Text.js app is a React app.

11
00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:37.350
Your components lay out with Flexbox,
into a grid of character cells.

12
00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:43.870
Each frame that changes becomes a single
console.log call, made of %c-styled spans.

13
00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:48.680
DevTools draws it in the console,
and the page only shows a focus pad.

14
00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.440
Let's create the app.

15
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:59.270
Scaffold a new project with
create-text-app, using the starter template.

16
00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:04.630
You get the App Router, TypeScript, and
the text CLI, in a handful of files.

17
00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:09.640
Move into the folder and install
dependencies, then start the dev server.

18
00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.470
Open localhost:3000.

19
00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.230
Then open the console.

20
00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:20.830
In Chrome that's ⌘⌥J, or
Ctrl+Shift+J on Windows and Linux.

21
00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.270
The page only shows a focus pad.

22
00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:25.760
Your app is in the console.

23
00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:31.000
Now, your first page.

24
00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:36.630
Every route is a page.tsx
file in the app folder.

25
00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:40.070
Replace the starter page with
the dashboard's title card.

26
00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:44.150
Box and Text come from @textjs/app.

27
00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.150
Box is a layout container.

28
00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:50.150
Its class names are Flexbox
utilities, measured in cells:

29
00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:55.030
a column with a rounded border, and
padding of two cells across and one down.

30
00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:59.190
Inside, a bold title, and a
line in the theme's muted color.

31
00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.390
Save the file.

32
00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:04.840
Fast Refresh redraws the frame,
and keeps your component state.

33
00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:10.080
Next, respond to a key.

34
00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:15.630
useInput receives every keystroke
while the page has focus.

35
00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:17.230
Let's count the hellos.

36
00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:22.830
Import useState from React, and
useInput alongside Box and Text.

37
00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:24.670
Keep the count in state.

38
00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:26.990
When the key is return, add one.

39
00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:29.790
When the input is r, reset to zero.

40
00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.960
Then show the count next to the greeting.

41
00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:38.350
Here it is, running in real
DevTools, on the lesson page.

42
00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:41.390
Click the pad first,
so the page has focus:

43
00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:44.910
keys typed into the DevTools
prompt never reach the page.

44
00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:47.870
Press Enter, and again, and again.

45
00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:50.110
Each press redraws the frame.

46
00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:53.200
Press r, and the count resets.

47
00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:58.480
That's a complete
Text.js app: React state,

48
00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:02.510
a layout box, and one
console.log per changed frame.

49
00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:07.870
Each key press changed a few cells, so
each one logged exactly one new frame.

50
00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:12.960
And while the app sits idle, nothing
changes, so nothing is logged at all.

51
00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:15.350
Quick check.

52
00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:19.080
Where does a Text.js app render its UI?

53
00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.030
In the DevTools console,
through console.log.

54
00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:28.400
Every changed frame is a
single log of styled spans.

55
00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:32.800
And what does an idle app log?

56
00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:35.250
Nothing.

57
00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:39.570
If no cell changed, the renderer
returns before it builds a string,

58
00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.780
so nothing is logged.

59
00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:48.380
Next, in chapter two, you'll build the
dashboard shell with Flexbox in cells:

60
00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:51.290
a top bar, a sidebar, and cards.

61
00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:52.940
See you there.
